// GPU-resident passes (card gpu-multipass). A field is a pair of targets that stay on the GPU: rgba16float
// where the device can render it, else rgba32float, else rgba8unorm. gpu_pass draws a fullscreen fragment
// into one field and swaps the pair. The passes of a frame share one command encoder, so nothing comes
// back to the CPU until gpu_picture. A shader reads field_<name>(uv), uv in 0..1, filtered when the format
// allows. gpu_show draws the last shader into the window (or the page canvas) and gpu_picture reads that
// one image back. Values are numbers and short vectors, the same holes paint fills ($width, $mouse, …).
gpu_fields(width: int, height: int, names: node): int from host
gpu_pass(shader: node, fields: int, into: node, values: node): int from host
gpu_show(shader: node, fields: int, values: node): int from host
gpu_picture(shader: node, fields: int, values: node): node from host
gpu_fields_format(): node from host
